libview - shared 3D view math for radioglobe and claudegraph
============================================================

libview is a small, pure-math library holding the code that
radioglobe (/usr/dave/work/radioglobe) and claudegraph
(/usr/dave/work/claude9/claudegraph.c) had each grown their own
diverging copy of.  It owns only numbers: no draw.h, no event.h,
no locking, no I/O.  The caller owns the event loop, the
projection style (radioglobe's orthographic disc vs claudegraph's
perspective), display locking, and rendering.

The contract is view.h.  It requires u.h and libc.h to be
included first (double, ulong, frand, sqrt, ...).

Contents
--------
  v3.c      Vec3 helpers: v3/v3add/v3sub/v3scale/v3dot/v3len and
            v3rand (uniform-direction vector, uses frand()).
            Ported from claudegraph's vadd/vsub/vmul/vdot/rndvec.

  orbit.c   viewbasis() -- the orbit-camera screen basis
            (ex/ey screen right/up, ez toward the viewer),
            identical to claudegraph's setview() and radioglobe's
            viewbasis() with yaw==lon, pitch==lat -- plus the
            Orbit inertial-drag state machine: orbitinit,
            orbitdown (grab stops spin), orbitmove (wrap-safe
            velocity across the +-180 seam), orbitup, orbittick
            (friction + vmin cutoff), orbitzoom, orbitnorm.

  spring.c  springdefaults + springstep, a force-directed graph
            layout: origin gravity, pairwise repulsion, edge
            springs, damped integration with a per-step speed cap
            and a |pos| clamp.  Faithful port of claudegraph's
            physstep() over Sbody pointers and an Sedge list.

  viewtest.c  Standalone test binary (no display) exercising the
              math; one PASS/FAIL line per check, exits nil iff
              all pass.

Consumers
---------
Two programs link this library:
  - claudegraph (/usr/dave/work/claude9), perspective projection.
  - radioglobe  (/usr/dave/work/radioglobe), orthographic globe.
Neither claude9fs, mkcoast, mkstations nor the other radioglobe
helpers link it.

Building
--------
    mk            build libview.a$O and viewtest
    mk clean      remove objects and outputs

The archive is libview.a$O (e.g. libview.a7 on arm64).  There is
deliberately no install target; deployment is the human's call.

Linking it into a consumer
--------------------------
Each consumer references the archive by absolute path from its own
mkfile, adds the include dir to CFLAGS, links the archive into the
affected binary only, and carries a virtual rule so a stale library
is rebuilt:

    LIBVIEW=/usr/dave/work/libview/libview.a$O
    CFLAGS=$CFLAGS -I/usr/dave/work/libview

    theprogram: $OFILES $LIBVIEW
        $LD -o $target $OFILES $LIBVIEW

    $LIBVIEW:V:
        @{cd /usr/dave/work/libview && mk}

Running the tests
-----------------
    mk viewtest
    ./6.viewtest        # or 7.viewtest etc., per $objtype

viewtest calls srand(1) first, so its output is deterministic.
It prints one "PASS name" or "FAIL name: detail" line per check
and exits nil only if every check passed.
